      {month:'2026-04',status:'NOTABLE',label:'Scattered Spider ringleader Buchanan pleads guilty (Apr 20)',detail:'Tyler Buchanan pleaded guilty in the Central District of California to wire fraud conspiracy and aggravated identity theft; in US custody, sentencing August 21, 2026. A custody outcome at the Western-affiliate edge of the ecosystem, where enforcement leverage actually exists.',conf:'CONFIRMED'},
      {month:'2026-05',status:'NOTABLE',label:'The Gentlemen: 8 affiliate TOX IDs exposed; AI-assisted RaaS dev; dual-leverage extortion tactic',detail:'Check Point Research (May 13) analysis of the May 4 Gentlemen backend breach identified: 8 distinct affiliate TOX IDs across 29 confirmed campaigns; most active affiliate (TOX 98C132E2...) ran 11 of 29 campaigns; 90/10 split model (90% to affiliate); approximately 9 named operators in leaked communications. Admin zeta88 plays dual role: manages platform, builds locker, runs payouts, AND directly conducts infections. AI-assisted development confirmed: GLOCKER RaaS panel built in 3 days using DeepSeek, Qwen, and Kimi, the first documented operational preference for Chinese LLMs over Western models in RaaS development. Operators discussing self-hosted uncensored LLMs for automated triage of exfiltrated victim data (planned, not yet deployed). Novel dual-leverage tactic documented: stolen data from Victim A reused to attack Victim B, then Victim A publicly attributed as access broker on DLS: cascading extortion pressure at zero additional intrusion cost.',conf:'CONFIRMED'},
      {month:'2026-05',status:'NOTABLE',label:'LockBit affiliate sentenced to 102 months',detail:'A Latvian LockBit affiliate was sentenced to 102 months in US federal court in May 2026. Single-source reporting.',conf:'CREDIBLE'},
      {month:'2026-06',status:'NOTABLE',label:'Jubair and Flowers plead guilty on day one of UK trial (Jun 26)',detail:'Thalha Jubair and Owen Flowers pleaded guilty at Woolwich Crown Court on the first day of trial over the Transport for London attack; Flowers also admitted US healthcare intrusions. Both await UK sentencing; Jubair faces outstanding US charges. Continues the pattern of custody outcomes concentrating at the Western-affiliate edge.',conf:'CONFIRMED'},
      {month:'2026-07',status:'NOTABLE',label:'Vardanyan (Ryuk deployer) pleads guilty (Jul 8); Scattered Spider suspect Stokes extradited (Jul 1)',detail:'Karen Vardanyan, extradited from Ukraine in 2025, pleaded guilty July 8 to conspiracy and computer fraud counts (up to 15 years); sentencing September 22, 2026. Tied to 2,400+ attacks and more than $15M in BTC extorted November 2019 to April 2020; custody achieved via the Ukraine extradition channel, with no current ecosystem effect since the Ryuk lineage is defunct. Separately, Scattered Spider suspect Peter Stokes was extradited from Finland July 1 and detained pending trial (roughly $8M extortion attempt, 100+ intrusions).',conf:'CONFIRMED'}
