      {month:'2026-05',status:'NOTABLE',label:'May ~700 victims est. (-9.4% MoM); 8 new groups debuted; RAMP 120+ days dark',detail:'May 2026 estimated ~700 victims (9.4% MoM decline from 772 confirmed in April; Source: Ransomware.live tracking; final count will update at month close). Decline directionally consistent with Operation Saffron/Stark infrastructure disruptions; seasonal variation and DLS publishing lag cannot be excluded. Cannot confirm whether groups are publishing fewer victims or publishing slower, which is analytically significant for ransom leverage assessment. 8 new groups debuted May: Fulcrumsec (23 victims), Leakbazaar (9), Blackwater (6), Cmdorganization (4), Prinzeugen (1), Icarus (1), Shadowbyt3$ (reactivated), Titan. YTD 2026: approximately 3,894 victims across 97 active groups and 119 countries. RAMP non-reconstitution at 120+ days is the single most anomalous structural signal: competing hypothesis is permanent private-channel migration, which reduces open-source DLS visibility.',conf:'CONFIRMED'},
      {month:'2026-06',status:'NOTABLE',label:'Data-only extortion consolidates: World Leaks, SRG, and ShinyHunters all encryption-free in June; ~22% of IR cases',detail:'World Leaks (Hunters International rebrand) listed Tata Electronics, an Apple contract manufacturer: 204,341 files / 630.4 GB (confirmed by BleepingComputer Jun 23). Silent Ransom Group reached roughly 100 listed victims, compressing end-to-end extortion to under one business day via vishing and in-person USB theft, with leak infrastructure on an 18-country, 22-ISP residential botnet to resist takedown (Mandiant/Resecurity). Best-available baseline: 22% of incident-response cases now run data-only, up roughly 11x year over year (primary source unverified).',conf:'CREDIBLE'},
      {month:'2026-07',status:'NOTABLE',label:'Encryption-free extortion hits a monetization ceiling: 15% exfiltration-only payment rate (Coveware Q2)',detail:'Average payment $1.88 million (+176% QoQ) against a $150,000 median and a record-low overall payment rate: the ecosystem is extracting far more from far fewer payers. The 15% exfil-only payment rate is the first hard quantitative evidence that data theft without encryption carries a structural monetization penalty. Named extortion-only actors in July: ShinyHunters (Abbott; Medtronic notification of 3.8M individuals unconfirmed), Kairos (~$1 million from a US county), World Leaks.',conf:'CONFIRMED'}
